# Sample B — Thin material

*What most submissions will actually look like.*

### 素材 (raw)

> **Agent:** Anything new this week?
>
> **Vendor (Dan, Hollow Ridge Farm):** Just the usual. Kale, chard, some late tomatoes.
>
> **Agent:** How are the tomatoes doing this late in the season?
>
> **Vendor:** Not great honestly. The rain last week split a lot of them. I lost maybe a third.
>
> **Agent:** What happens to the split ones?
>
> **Vendor:** I usually feed them to the pigs but there were too many. So I've been making sauce. Never sold sauce before.
>
> **Agent:** How much sauce?
>
> **Vendor:** Thirty something jars. I don't have a label or anything, I wrote on masking tape.

**Signals:** person ✓ · stake ✓ · change ✓ · scene ✗ · quotes ✗

### Draft — 112 words

**Headline:** A third of the tomatoes split. Now there's sauce.

The rain last week split about a third of Dan's late tomatoes. Split tomatoes don't sell.

Normally they go to the pigs. There were too many for the pigs.

So there is sauce now — thirty-something jars of it, which Hollow Ridge has never made before and never sold. The jars are labeled in marker on masking tape.

Kale and chard as usual. The sauce is at the end of the table.

**Assessment: ✅ Clears the bar, at the shorter length.**
Something went wrong, someone responded, there's a concrete image in the masking tape. No quote, so it's slot 5 material rather than slot 2. **This is the realistic median and it's fine.**

